fixes Segmentation fault

```js
import { Database } from "bun:sqlite";
const db = new Database(":memory:")
const stmt = db.prepare("select 1")
db.close()
console.log(stmt.all()) //succeeds
console.log(stmt.get()) //succeeds
console.log(stmt.run()) //Segmentation fault!! , should be: "Database has closed" or "Cannot use a closed database"
```
https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/98f9e276b032a139ef341a69e7967824718390bb/src/bun.js/bindings/sqlite/JSSQLStatement.cpp

once you close the db, `version_db->db` will be `nullptr`
```c++
databases()[dbIndex]->db = nullptr;
```
`stmt.run()`
```c++
int total_changes_before = sqlite3_total_changes(castedThis->version_db->db);
```

https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/98f9e276b032a139ef341a69e7967824718390bb/src/bun.js/bindings/sqlite/sqlite3.c
```c++
return db->nTotalChange;
```

___

this also happens when `db` is garbage collected:

https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/98f9e276b032a139ef341a69e7967824718390bb/src/bun.js/bindings/sqlite/JSSQLStatement.cpp
```c++
databases()[index]->db = nullptr;
```


```js
import { context } from 'esbuild' //"esbuild": "^0.20.2"
import { Database } from "bun:sqlite";

//I wasn't able to get `db` garbage collected without importing `esbuild` and using it
const ctx = await context({
    entryPoints: [],
    outdir: 'www/js',
    bundle: true,
    write: false,
    sourcemap: 'inline',
})

function get_stmt() {
    const db = new Database(":memory:")
    const stmt = db.prepare("select 1")
    return stmt
}
const stmt = get_stmt()

setTimeout(() => {
    console.log(stmt.run());
}, 2000);
```

___

my changes are to add a CHECK only to the `.run` method, and not the `.all` nor the `.get` method, since they seem to work even if the database is closed

for `.run` to keep working, `sqlite3_total_changes()` would have to be skipped, and `.changes` would have to always be `0`, which would potentially break users' if statements depending on this

___

for the garbage collection part, I'm using reference counting on `VersionSqlite3`.. I don't know of a better solution yet,

